posts.body:
So I did it, and was I glad I did!
In this video I play the whole demo for the above mentioned "The Silent Kingdom" by
@LuckyCatOtome
. It wasn't too talky-talky for my taste. Some of the dialogue is a little verbose, but that's kind of expected of the way royalty would speak. I absolutely loved this one. Some of the QTEs are a little hard to time right because I'm not exactly sure when during the animations would be the ideal spot to press the button and kind of feels like guessing but overall I didn't mind. The art is absolutely gorgeous, the game runs flawlessly, and the story leaves you wanting so much more. I really really enjoyed this one and thanks to
@MoztheTiger
for suggesting it!

@Timespiraled_RPG
sorry it took me a bit. I didnt know what to do at first but once I got it I found it intriguing and very unique!
@woootbm
I know you've already seen it but here you go, bro.
@Kyuubits
I love the custom art and the story was very moving.
